    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Retirement",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S4253\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act granting retroactive membership in the New\nYork state and local employees' retirement system to Adam Markel\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nThis bill would grant Adam Markel Tier 2 status in the New York State\nPolice and Fire Retirement system upon application.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1: Authorizes Adam Markel to apply for retroactive membership\nin the New York State and Local Employees' Retirement System with an\neffective date of September 5, 2006. Once an application is filed with\nthe head of the New York State Police and Fire Retirement system,\nwithin one year from the effective date of this act, such service\ncredit will be transferred.\n\nSection 2 states that no contributions made to the New York state\nPolice and Fire Retirement System by Adam Markel should be returned or\nrefunded to him.\n\nSection 3 states that all past service costs of implementing the\nprovisions of this act shall be borne by the State University of New\nYork at Buffalo.\n\nSection 4: Provides that this act shall take effect immediately.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nAdam Markel was a part-time employee with the State University of New\nYork at Buffalo from September 5, 2006 until April 14, 2009. However,\nthrough no fault of his own, he did not become a member of the New\nYork State and Local Employees' Retirement System during that time.\nThis legislation would afford Mr. Markel the ability to establish\nmembership in the retirement system as of September 5, 2006 thereby\ncorrecting this oversight. It should be noted that all past service\ncosts of implementing the provisions of this act would be borne by the\nState University of New York at Buffalo.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\n2015-16: S.7111/A.9703 Passed Senate/Referred to Governmental\nEmployees\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nSee fiscal note.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
